From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:52:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: Claude Agent (Plus)'s Plan updates is a ToDo toggle
 in the agent menu

The adapter's `plan_updates` session option turns on the CLI's todo tools,
so the plan view fills on current models. Zed drew it in the composer row
beside Model, Effort and Mode, as it draws every boolean option. That row
holds per-turn choices; this one is set once per thread, and its name
described the mechanism rather than what the user sees, which is the
agent's todo list.

What changes:

  * The option leaves the composer row (`shows_in_composer_row`). It is
    matched by its id, `plan_updates` -- the id the adapter keeps so saved
    defaults still match, whatever name it advertises.
  * The agent panel's options menu ("Toggle Agent Menu", the ellipsis) gets a
    checkable "ToDo" entry under "Current Thread". It shows from the first
    message on, not only once the thread has messages like the entries
    beside it: the toggle decides whether that first turn already fills the
    plan view. Disabled when the session's options are read-only; absent
    when the agent does not offer the option.
  * The state is read when the menu opens, not when the panel last
    rendered, so a toggle shows on reopen without a panel repaint. It comes
    from the root thread: the option belongs to the session, and a subagent
    thread in focus shares it.
  * Toggling is thread-local, like the composer switch it replaces and like
    cycling: no default is saved, because the adapter scopes the option to
    the session (claude-agent-plus `plan-updates.ts`).
  * Both shapes are handled: the native boolean, and the "on"/"off" select
    the adapter sends to a client without boolean options.

The label is fixed here ("ToDo") rather than taken from the adapter, so the
entry reads the same against an adapter that still advertises "Plan
updates"; claude-agent-plus renames it to "ToDo" in the same change.

Tests (config_options::tests): the toggle flips both shapes and saves no
default; an agent without the option gets no entry and no request; the
option leaves the composer row while other booleans stay.

Packaging: claude-agent-acp-plus group, after 0072. It follows 0010's rule
that a gesture moves the thread and only Shift-confirm saves a default, and
the only agent that offers the option is that adapter.
---

